xnu 0158: verify the touch SPI half period and the firmware split

The bit-bang asked for 800 ns a half period and got 103 us because the
tick count came from ml_get_timebase(); 0156 fixes the conversion. Print
the last SPI frame with the timebase value, the cost of a raw TLMM read
and of mach_absolute_time (per access), and split every firmware section
into the 4 KB write and the ack wait. A correct boot shows the frame at
tens of microseconds and write/ack in the hundreds of milliseconds.
